---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import InstallSection from "../../components/InstallSection.astro";
import SheetContent from "@ui/concepts/sheet.mdx";
import Component from "../../components/Component.astro";

import { SheetDemo, SheetManualDemo } from "../../demos/sheet-demo";

const title = "Sheet";
const description = "Interactive Sheet demo running the site's built registry source via an Astro island, with install and per-style usage from the package docs.";
---

<MainLayout frontmatter={{ title, description }}>
  <h1>Sheet</h1>
  <p>A side panel sliding in from any screen edge with an overlay, a built-in X close button, and wired title and description - the caller owns the open signal, the component wires everything else.</p>

  <InstallSection entry="sheet" />

  <Component heading="Playground" Demo={<SheetDemo client:load />} code="SheetDemo">
    <p>Slides in from the right with wired title and description, an X close button, escape and outside dismissal, and a focus trap.</p>
  </Component>
  <Component heading="Manual parts" Demo={<SheetManualDemo client:load />} code="SheetManualDemo">
    <p>The bottom side composed from the exported parts: overlay and panel portaled by hand, both fed the state accessor, the X close calling your onClose.</p>
  </Component>

  <SheetContent />
</MainLayout>
